From 07a0dd02b8a4d4a29175b8dbce75530771f7c083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:26:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban-sync): Board push channel and event-driven rounds
 [daveey]

Cross-gateway changes took about 10 s (5 s polling on both ends). The sync
loop now holds the Board's WebSocket feed per synced board (gateway key,
ping every 25 s, reconnect with backoff; optional: without websockets it
polls) and runs a round as soon as a change frame arrives, or within 0.5 s
of a local write landing in an outbox, else at the poll period.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
